IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-death`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 12 to 16, with the working beside each assertion.

§ `Regulations s 12 -- tests`

-- The three named kinds of person must notify, once the beneficiary has died; nobody else
-- is bound by s 12; and nobody is bound while the beneficiary is alive.
#ASSERT `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` TRUE `executor or administrator of the estate`
#ASSERT `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` TRUE `liquidator of the succession`
#ASSERT `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` TRUE `heir`
#ASSERT NOT `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` TRUE `none of these`
#ASSERT NOT `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` FALSE `heir`

§ `Regulations s 13 -- tests`

-- 13(1): died and did not receive that month's payment: eligible. Died and received it: not.
#ASSERT `the estate or succession or the heirs are eligible to receive the allocation payment for the month of death` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the estate or succession or the heirs are eligible to receive the allocation payment for the month of death` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the estate or succession or the heirs are eligible to receive the allocation payment for the month of death` FALSE FALSE
-- 13(2): to the estate or heirs, or if no heirs to the person or agency the Minister designates.
#ASSERT `who receives an amount owing on the death of a beneficiary` TRUE EQUALS `the beneficiary's estate or succession or the beneficiary's heirs`
#ASSERT `who receives an amount owing on the death of a beneficiary` FALSE EQUALS `a person or agency designated by the Minister`

§ `Regulations s 14 -- tests`

-- 14(1): disappeared and the Minister concludes the presumption arises.
#ASSERT `the Minister may determine the date on which the beneficiary's death is presumed to have occurred` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may determine the date on which the beneficiary's death is presumed to have occurred` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may determine the date on which the beneficiary's death is presumed to have occurred` FALSE TRUE
-- The deemed date wins over the actual one; without a determination the actual date stands.
#ASSERT `the date of death for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 5 9)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `the date of death for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 5 9)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 9)
#ASSERT `the date of death for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `the date of death for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 14(2) and 14(3): either a different date or news that the beneficiary is alive.
#ASSERT `the Minister must pay any benefit that would have been payable had the first determination not been made` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Minister must pay any benefit that would have been payable had the first determination not been made` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must pay any benefit that would have been payable had the first determination not been made` FALSE FALSE

§ `Regulations ss 15 and 16 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the representative may act on the person's behalf` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the representative may act on the person's behalf` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the representative may act on the person's behalf` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on the beneficiary's behalf to their representative` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on the beneficiary's behalf to their representative` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on the beneficiary's behalf to their representative` FALSE TRUE
